---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const description = 'About Mick’s evidence-led work in systems, automation, local AI, Linux and practical infrastructure.';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" {description} canonicalPath="/about/">
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">About Mick</p>
      <h1>Hands-on systems thinking, carried into software.</h1>
      <p class="lead">A technically capable career changer doing substantial practical work in systems, automation, local AI, reliability, governance, Linux and infrastructure.</p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="section-index">Background</p>
        <h2>From physical systems to digital ones.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Mick’s background is in practical industrial work, including manufacturing, mining and mechanical environments. That experience shows up in the current practice: find the actual failure, understand the boundary, preserve evidence, and do not call a job finished because the dashboard looks green.</p>
        <p>The transition into technical work has produced working systems, not a perpetual beginner narrative. The portfolio is careful about titles, though. It describes demonstrated work without claiming that Mick personally typed every implementation line or adopting a title that the public record has not established.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="section-index">Working method</p>
        <h2>AI-assisted, human-directed.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Mick identifies problems, designs constraints and authority boundaries, directs implementation campaigns, and decides what evidence is sufficient for acceptance. AI systems perform substantial implementation, analysis and review within that structure.</p>
        <p>That split is a strength only when it remains explicit. Model output is treated as evidence to inspect—not authority to obey. Consequential decisions, scope changes and publication stay human.</p>
        <ul class="focus-list">
          <li>System and workflow design</li>
          <li>Automation and deterministic validation</li>
          <li>Linux and local-AI operations</li>
          <li>Knowledge governance and provenance</li>
          <li>Creative-production systems</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="section-index">This site</p>
        <h2>The Sanctum</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>The Sanctum is the repository codename for this portfolio. Publicly, it is Mick’s Foundry: a static record of the work, its status and its inspectable public evidence. The implementation uses Astro and is prepared for GitHub Pages.</p>
        <div class="button-row">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="/work/">Explore the work</a>
          <a class="button" href="https://github.com/necromilias">GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
